---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import profile from '../data/profile.json';

const facebook = profile.social[0];
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy · Prof. Dr. Ali Mohamed Salah"
  description="What this website does and does not collect about its visitors."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  updated="2 November 2026"
>
  <p>
    This is the official website of Prof. Dr. Ali Mohamed Salah (Oslo, Norway). It has no accounts and no comments. The
    only place it asks for personal information is the contact form, and only if you choose to write.
  </p>

  <h2>What is collected</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Nothing by default.</strong> Fonts and images are served from this site itself, and no cookie is set until you
      choose.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Visit statistics, only if you accept.</strong> The cookie notice asks whether we may count visits. If you accept,
      the site loads Vercel Web Analytics, which counts page views, the page you came from, your country, browser and
      device type. It does not use cookies and does not follow you from site to site. If you decline, it is not loaded.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The contact form, only if you send it.</strong> Your name, email address, topic and message are emailed to
      the inbox that answers this website's messages, so they can be read and answered. The message passes through Resend, the service that
      delivers the email, and is kept in that mailbox for as long as the correspondence needs. The website itself
      stores nothing.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Server logs.</strong> Our host, Vercel Inc., processes your IP address and request details to deliver the
      pages and keep the site secure, as any web host does.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your choice</h2>
  <p>
    Your answer to the cookie notice is kept in your own browser (local storage, key <code>cookie-consent</code>). To change
    it, clear this site's data in your browser and the notice will appear again.
  </p>

  <h2>Other websites</h2>
  <p>
    Lecture pictures are loaded from YouTube (Google), so Google receives your IP address when you view them. Links to
    YouTube, Facebook and Amazon lead to sites with their own privacy policies; we do not control them.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under the GDPR you may ask what is held about you, and ask for it to be corrected or deleted. A message you sent
    through the contact form is held in the inbox that received it; write through the contact page to have it deleted.
    Beyond that the site holds no personal data except what its host logs, so other requests usually concern Vercel. You may also complain to the Norwegian
    Data Protection Authority (Datatilsynet).
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy can be sent through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> or the official <a href={facebook.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Facebook page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
